# HIGH SEAS - a sea-shanty jig, and the song that counts in six instead of four.
# The format is in Demo1/CLAUDE.md, under "Song files". Instruments are tables with
# one entry per frame; each channel holds named tracks of 12 rows; the lines at the
# end are the order list. In a track '.' holds and '-' releases. '#' starts a comment.
#
# An original tune in an old idiom: the jig, in 6/8 - two beats a bar, three eighth
# notes a beat. Every other song here is 4/4 in sixteenths, sixteen rows a line. This
# one says 'rows 12' and 'beat 3': a row is an eighth note, a line is two bars, and the
# tracker page lights every third row instead of every fourth.
#
# The pirate sound is the idiom, not any one tune: a minor key, a fiddle running in
# eighths, a squeezebox pumping on the off-beats, an oom-pah bass and a stomp and a clap
# on deck. A minor because the bass lives on the buzz table, and A, D, E, F and G# all
# land within 11 cents on it. G misses by 19, so there is no G chord - the harmony is
# A minor, D minor, E and F - and C misses by 31, so F's bass rocks between octaves
# rather than out to its fifth.

song   HIGH SEAS
key    A MINOR
rows   12
beat   3

# The kick and snare Guardian uses: a falling thump on the buzz table, and a crack of
# tone into noise. With AUDCTL at $00 the snare is plain 17-bit hiss.
instrument KICK
  table      none
  volume     15 14 13 11 9 7 5 3 1 0
  distortion tone buzz
  audf       40 20 27 34 43 52 62 71 80
  release    2

instrument SNARE
  table      none
  volume     13 12 10 8 6 5 4 3 2 1 0
  distortion tone noise
  audf       50 6 7 8 9 10 11 12 13
  release    2

# The bass: plucked, and gone before the next beat, so the oom-pah is separate notes.
instrument OOM
  table      buzz
  volume     11 10 8 7 6 5 4 3
  distortion buzz
  release    3

# The fiddle: bowed in rather than struck - a level under full on the first frame - and
# vibrato only on a note held past eight frames, so the running eighths stay clean and
# the long notes sing.
instrument FIDDLE
  table      tone
  volume     10 12 12 11 11 10 10 10 9
  distortion tone
  vibrato    0 1 1 0 -1 -1
  delay      8
  release    2

# The squeezebox: each chord an arpeggio, pumped - in and out inside one eighth note, so
# two in a row are two pushes of the bellows rather than one held chord.
instrument SQUEEZE
  table      tone
  volume     8 8 7 6 5 4 2 1 0
  distortion tone
  release    2

channel 1 drums DECK
  note  A stomp on the first beat of the bar and a clap on the second - 6/8's two
  note  beats, three rows apart. The second stomp track adds the pickups a crew stamping
  note  in time would, and the roll runs the last bar of the turnaround into the top.
  kit   K=KICK S=SNARE
  track INTRO  K . .  . . .  K . .  . . .
  track STOMP  K . .  S . .  K . .  S . .
  track STOMP2 K . .  S . .  K . K  S . S
  track ROLL   K . .  S . .  S S S  S S S

channel 2 notes BASS
  note  Oom-pah in six: the root on the first beat, the fifth on the second. F has no
  note  usable fifth - C is 31 cents out on distortion C - so its bars rock between F1
  note  and F2, and the E bars swing to the third, G#, instead of out to B.
  voice OOM
  track AM  A1 . .  E2 . .  A1 . .  E2 . .
  track AE  A1 . .  E2 . .  E2 . .  G#1 . .
  track DE  D2 . .  A1 . .  E2 . .  G#1 . .
  track DEA D2 . .  E2 . .  A1 . E2  A1 . .
  track FF  F1 . .  F2 . .  F1 . .  F2 . .
  track DD  D2 . .  A1 . .  D2 . .  A1 . .
  track EE  E2 . .  G#1 . .  E2 . .  G#1 . .

channel 3 notes FIDDLE
  note  The tune. The jig is quarter-and-eighth against runs of three: a leap up the
  note  chord and a run back down. The shanty answers in long calls, a dotted quarter
  note  each, with the vibrato arriving on them, and a run to finish each bar.
  voice FIDDLE
  track PICK  . . .  . . .  . . .  D5 C5 B4
  track A1    E5 . C5  A4 . C5  E5 D5 C5  B4 . A4
  track A2    D5 . A4  F4 . A4  G#4 A4 B4  E4 . .
  track A3    E5 . C5  A4 . C5  E5 F5 E5  D5 C5 B4
  track A4    F5 . D5  B4 . G#4  A4 . E4  A4 . .
  track B1    A5 . .  F5 . .  C5 D5 E5  F5 . C5
  track B2    E5 . .  C5 . .  A4 B4 C5  E5 . .
  track B3    F5 . .  D5 . .  A4 . D5  F5 E5 D5
  track B4    E5 . .  B4 . .  G#4 A4 B4  D5 C5 B4
  track TURN  A4 . .  - . .  E4 G#4 B4  D5 C5 B4

channel 4 notes SQUEEZEBOX
  note  The off-beats: the second and third eighth of every beat, the bass taking the
  note  first. That pattern - bass, chord, chord - is what makes six-eight lilt.
  voice SQUEEZE
  track CAM  . Am Am  . Am Am  . Am Am  . Am Am
  track CAE  . Am Am  . Am Am  . E E  . E E
  track CDE  . Dm Dm  . Dm Dm  . E E  . E E
  track CDEA . Dm Dm  . E E  . Am Am  . Am Am
  track CF   . F F  . F F  . F F  . F F
  track CDM  . Dm Dm  . Dm Dm  . Dm Dm  . Dm Dm
  track CE   . E E  . E E  . E E  . E E

# The order list: one line per two bars, a track per channel, '.' for none.
# Deck, bass, fiddle, squeezebox.
section CAST OFF
speed  11
audctl $00
line   INTRO  AM     .      CAM
line   INTRO  AE     PICK   CAE
loop
section JIG
line   STOMP  AM     A1     CAM
line   STOMP  DE     A2     CDE
line   STOMP  AM     A3     CAM
line   STOMP  DEA    A4     CDEA
section SHANTY
line   STOMP  FF     B1     CF
line   STOMP  AM     B2     CAM
line   STOMP  DD     B3     CDM
line   STOMP  EE     B4     CE
section JIG
line   STOMP2 AM     A1     CAM
line   STOMP2 DE     A2     CDE
line   STOMP2 AM     A3     CAM
line   STOMP2 DEA    A4     CDEA
section TURNAROUND
line   ROLL   AE     TURN   CAE
